WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:02.310
Tianran: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:03.900
we wanted to find all the differences

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.690
between McDonald's in the US and China.

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:08.667
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:12.867
New season, USA versus China.

00:00:12.867 --> 00:00:14.670
I'm so excited for you guys to see this

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:17.730
and to meet our new cohost, Tianran.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:20.162
USA versus China, let's go.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.440
Drinks from McDonald's in
China come in three sizes,

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:28.350
small, medium, and big.

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:32.520
But for some reason the
medium is 444 milliliters,

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:36.840
which in Chinese basically
just means die, die, die,

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:38.010
which is just super unlucky,

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:39.840
so I guess they really
want you to either get

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.610
the large or the small.

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:44.220
The drinks at a US
McDonald's come four sizes,

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:46.110
the extra small, where'd it go?

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:47.310
Sorry, they forgot it.

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:50.520
The small, the medium, and the large.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:54.028
Our large is 80.9% bigger

00:00:54.028 --> 00:00:56.078
than China's largest soda.

00:00:56.078 --> 00:00:57.660
Let's see if that's true.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:59.493
Bound to be a little bit in the lid.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.920
That is blasphemous!

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.710
Shame these people. Shame this clown.

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:10.260
Some of you over the past several years

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:11.947
have said something to the tune of,

00:01:11.947 --> 00:01:13.380
it doesn't count or it's wrong

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:15.660
because we add the ice, or
we keep the ice in there,

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:16.835
and that isn't a true measurement,

00:01:16.835 --> 00:01:18.935
which I don't believe, but fine.

00:01:18.935 --> 00:01:20.400
For the first time ever,

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.380
I want to measure this without the ice.

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:25.110
I'm solving this once and for all.

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:27.480
So, right away you get even less soda.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:32.010
Let's get this up to
exactly 32 fluid ounces.

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:33.690
32 ounces of Coca-Cola

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:38.070
in the supposed 32-ounce McDonald's cup.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:39.870
I'm so sick of this.

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:43.710
Why are they saying 32 fluid ounces?

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:47.700
Look! Just say 30 or 31. It's fine.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:48.930
Your move, McDonald's.

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:50.963
Our fries come in three sizes:

00:01:50.963 --> 00:01:53.096
small, medium, and large.

00:01:53.096 --> 00:01:55.020
American fries come in three sizes:

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:57.480
small, medium, and large.

00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:59.943
We will now weigh our largest fry.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:02.190
So, what about McNuggets?

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:04.050
Here in China, you can only get them

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:06.510
as an order of five or 10,

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:09.210
which is really just two portions of five.

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:10.950
That's cute, China. Real cute.

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:14.610
Here in the US, we have way
many more nugget options.

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:16.609
Four-piece, for your infant,

00:02:16.609 --> 00:02:19.260
six-piece, 10-piece, 20-piece,

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:22.260
and our largest, the 40-piece.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.660
All the mathheads watching
will be quick to point out

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:29.660
that this is 300% of
China's largest portion.

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:34.830
So, here are all the McDonald's
menu items from China

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:36.630
that you won't find in the US.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:39.060
Here are all the
McDonald's items in the US

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:40.360
you won't find in China.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.240
Oh, my God, I've been
staring at this for so long.

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:44.400
This is incredible. Check out the back!

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.400
It's an origami apple! This is the best.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.720
Let's see what we got.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:51.136
A hamburger, mini fries,

00:02:51.136 --> 00:02:54.300
a drink, a corn cup.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:57.210
[gasps] Dun-dun-dun!

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.676
Po!

00:02:58.676 --> 00:03:02.434
Oh, my God, this is way
better than the Hamburglar.

00:03:02.434 --> 00:03:05.220
What? do I have to build Po as well?

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:08.580
This is -- [laughs] I'm too old for this.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.290
Anyway, if you don't want a hamburger,

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:13.230
you can also change this
out for a fish fillet

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:15.540
or for four pieces of nuggets.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:20.340
You can also get the corn cup
changed out for apple slices,

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:23.043
but they will cost you 1 kuai extra.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:28.170
And with the juice, you can
have either apple juice,

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:30.120
milk, or water.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:33.690
So only healthy options
here in China's McDonald's.

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:35.130
OK, now on to the toy.

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:36.805
So, this is going to take
a while. Give me a second.

00:03:36.805 --> 00:03:37.638
Ugh.

00:03:37.638 --> 00:03:41.121
And then something flips
out from behind his groin.

00:03:41.121 --> 00:03:44.407
In here! It's coming together!

00:03:44.407 --> 00:03:46.715
Oh!

00:03:46.715 --> 00:03:48.998
It's a basketball hoop.

00:03:48.998 --> 00:03:52.060
Oh, my God, this is ingenuity at its best.

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:53.850
Look, we can play hoops with this.

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:55.841
Three, two, one!

00:03:55.841 --> 00:03:57.782
Whoa!

00:03:57.782 --> 00:04:01.380
I noticed that his Happy
Meal, even the box was a toy.

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:04.080
In America, our Happy Meal box

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:06.510
is another opportunity
for an advertisement.

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:09.720
All-new season of "The Masked
Singer" on Fox. Check it out.

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:12.630
Jesus, they're shameless. These kids.

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:15.390
Remember before, the
extra-small fry? Found it.

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:17.385
More nuggets, a four-piece.

00:04:17.385 --> 00:04:18.960
Apple slices.

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:21.760
Our toy is decidedly not a puzzle.

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:24.360
Remember when Kermit
the Frog was in there?

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:25.620
That was weird.

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:26.700
OK, what is this?

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:28.890
Who? What celebrity was the fox?

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:30.420
Oh, it was Wayne Brady.
OK, I've heard of him.

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:32.490
What, is his head in here?

00:04:32.490 --> 00:04:33.960
Oddly enough, shows the stark difference

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:35.220
between China and the US.

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:36.960
Theirs has this puzzle to put together,

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:38.837
ours is an ad for a TV show.

00:04:38.837 --> 00:04:42.087
[laughs and cries]

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:47.100
OK, so these are our
exclusive beef burgers.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:50.580
Here in China, people mostly eat pork,

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:51.990
so I think with the beef

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:54.690
they've really had to
go the premium route,

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:56.520
so you've got some
interesting combinations.

00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:00.300
This is the German sausage
double beef burger,

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:03.120
but in Chinese the name is kind of like

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:06.090
the "anti-vegetarian tyrant."

00:05:06.090 --> 00:05:09.390
So they've got some pretty
aggressive marketing for this.

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:13.685
Imagine Terry Crews just
pulsing his pecks while he --

00:05:13.685 --> 00:05:15.090
what is that?

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:16.240
Ugh.

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:19.148
If this is what they
call a German sausage,

00:05:19.148 --> 00:05:21.510
then I think the Germans
will be very angry.

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:24.843
Here we've got a BLT double beef burger.

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:28.862
I'm so sad. What is this?

00:05:28.862 --> 00:05:30.420
This is like a BLT sandwich

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:33.420
that's been sat at the bottom
of your bag for a week.

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:34.980
I'm excited about these, though.

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:39.450
These are the Angus
max thick beef burgers.

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:42.360
Now, McDonald's have done
premium collaborations

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:44.820
with Michelin-starred chefs in the past,

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:48.360
and they even have these
really super-fancy packaging.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:51.495
Look at that. Double cheeseburger.

00:05:51.495 --> 00:05:55.860
Oh, wow! Look at that.

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:58.500
The meat patty is thicker than my thumb.

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:00.219
That's a proper burger.

00:06:00.219 --> 00:06:01.485
Mm.

00:06:01.485 --> 00:06:04.326
Well, it's very meaty. Incredibly cheesy.

00:06:04.326 --> 00:06:06.870
This is the double cheeseburger,
so I can understand that.

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:08.610
For the vast majority of Chinese people,

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:12.180
their understanding or
access to Western food

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:14.160
may really come from
fast-food restaurants.

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:17.670
So this is probably the
gourmet burger experience

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:20.070
for the vast majority of
the Chinese population.

00:06:20.070 --> 00:06:23.790
In the US, you can get a
Quarter Pounder with cheese.

00:06:23.790 --> 00:06:26.160
What the heck? They gave us two tops?

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:27.540
This is the special two-top

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:29.070
Quarter Pounder with cheese, apparently.

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:31.770
And we also have a double Quarter Pounder,

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:33.360
if you want to increase the meat.

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:35.130
If someone wants to get
their daily vegetables,

00:06:35.130 --> 00:06:37.560
here is the Quarter
Pounder with cheese deluxe.

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:38.910
Swimming in mayonnaise.

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:40.800
We have something in the United
States called the McDouble.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.530
If you want slightly less
cheese on a double cheeseburger,

00:06:43.530 --> 00:06:44.363
we got you covered.

00:06:44.363 --> 00:06:45.570
Quarter Pounder with bacon.

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:46.980
Every once in a while, they
just take a Quarter Pounder

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:47.940
and put bacon on it,

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:50.160
and they repackage it for a celebrity.

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:54.090
And these are our exclusive
chicken and fish options.

00:06:54.090 --> 00:06:55.440
So, I want to start you off with this,

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:59.760
which has since become
McDonald's best spicy burger.

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:02.730
This is the McSpicy chicken fillet.

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:07.072
Apparently it's 1,000 SHU,

00:07:07.072 --> 00:07:08.980
which is a Scoville unit,

00:07:08.980 --> 00:07:12.330
and it's roughly equivalent
to the spiciness you get

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:14.130
from a spicy and numbing hot pot,

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:16.380
and those guys are pretty spicy.

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:18.180
Mm. Oh, that's delicious.

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:19.680
You don't feel the burn at first,

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:21.930
and then it's like your tongue
slowly starts to wake up,

00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:23.850
and it's like a frog in a pot.

00:07:23.850 --> 00:07:26.310
It slowly starts to realize
it's being boiled alive,

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:28.018
and by the end of this burger,

00:07:28.018 --> 00:07:29.193
you're going to want that Coke.

00:07:29.193 --> 00:07:33.810
Now, this is McDonald's
best-selling non-spicy burger,

00:07:33.810 --> 00:07:35.670
the grilled chicken sandwich,

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:37.980
which supposedly has no growth hormones

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:39.080
in their chicken feed.

00:07:40.530 --> 00:07:43.380
Very heavy on the black
pepper. Oh. Ooh, wow.

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:44.430
I'm very excited about this.

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:47.130
This is the McCrunch
chicken fillet burger,

00:07:47.130 --> 00:07:49.989
and in Chinese the name is "katsusui."

00:07:49.989 --> 00:07:52.290
It sounds like how it's supposed to taste.

00:07:52.290 --> 00:07:54.270
"Ka" is kind of like "crunchy,"

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:56.200
and "tsu" is kind of like

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:58.230
the juice kind of squirting out.

00:07:58.230 --> 00:08:02.718
So this should be both crunchy and juicy.

00:08:02.718 --> 00:08:06.513
Ooh, that looks like a much
better piece of chicken.

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:10.240
Yes, yes.

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:12.390
I didn't get the "ka,"

00:08:12.390 --> 00:08:14.430
probably because this has gone a bit cold,

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:17.157
but look at that. It is juicy in there.

00:08:17.157 --> 00:08:20.405
OK, this is the
super-spicy chicken fillet.

00:08:20.405 --> 00:08:21.450
Look at this guy!

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:23.942
You know this is going to
be super spicy. It's orange!

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:30.277
It's not that spicy.

00:08:30.277 --> 00:08:32.443
[coughs] Ooh!

00:08:32.443 --> 00:08:34.830
It's not as -- oh!

00:08:34.830 --> 00:08:37.020
Oh, my God.

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:38.078
Very tasty.

00:08:38.078 --> 00:08:41.130
Finish that, and it's

00:08:41.130 --> 00:08:42.780
to the hospital you go. Whew.

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:47.340
And last but, in my opinion,
least, the double fish burger.

00:08:47.340 --> 00:08:49.770
Chicken sandwiches.

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:51.960
There's something that is new-ish,

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:53.733
the bacon ranch McCrispy.

00:08:54.987 --> 00:08:56.487
Hm.

00:08:56.487 --> 00:08:57.495
It's just OK.

00:08:57.495 --> 00:09:00.120
There's also a bacon
ranch deluxe McCrispy,

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:01.650
where deluxe equals more vegetables.

00:09:01.650 --> 00:09:05.460
The McCrispy is something that
we ordered and they forgot.

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:07.650
And then now, piling on the vegetables,

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:09.600
you got the McCrispy deluxe.

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:11.190
Spicy McCrispy.

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:13.177
So they just rebranded the
crispy chicken sandwich

00:09:13.177 --> 00:09:14.618
to be the McCrispy?

00:09:15.584 --> 00:09:18.251
How spicy can this be?
This is not spicy at all.

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:25.860
So, McDonald's China has one roll option,

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:29.268
which is this crispy pork and

00:09:29.268 --> 00:09:31.801
pickled bamboo shoot wrap.

00:09:33.832 --> 00:09:35.340
Mm.

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:36.600
That's tasty. It's nice and crunchy.

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:39.873
Very spicy! [laughs] Wow.

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:42.205
Mm.

00:09:42.205 --> 00:09:43.746
It's spicy. It's sour.

00:09:43.746 --> 00:09:46.640
Anything that has Sichuan peppercorn in it

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:47.760
is just incredible.

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:50.010
Here we've got the McSpicy wings,

00:09:50.010 --> 00:09:54.260
which come in portions of two, four,

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:56.051
or nine.

00:09:56.051 --> 00:09:57.600
Straight up, I wish we had those wings.

00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:58.860
Those wings look really good.

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:00.480
Also, I don't know if you've noticed,

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:03.720
but the decoration here on the packet,

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:04.710
this is a collaboration

00:10:04.710 --> 00:10:08.940
with a streetwear brand
called Clot, or C-L-O-T,

00:10:08.940 --> 00:10:12.180
and it uses traditional
Chinese aesthetics.

00:10:12.180 --> 00:10:14.430
So here you've got the lucky knot,

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:18.060
which is sort of like a symbol
for good luck and longevity.

00:10:18.060 --> 00:10:19.230
As Chinese as it gets.

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:22.890
And this is also the same
flavor as the McSpicy burger.

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:25.770
I don't know if there's an
accurate translation for this.

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:28.103
This is literally called

00:10:28.103 --> 00:10:31.503
"such a big chicken chop."

00:10:31.503 --> 00:10:35.603
It's about the same size as
my palm, a little bit bigger.

00:10:35.603 --> 00:10:37.323
The McCrispy chicken.

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:40.620
Mm. Crispy, wow.

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:42.150
Mm, yes!

00:10:42.150 --> 00:10:45.870
This is very special.

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:47.910
We didn't think we'd be
able to get this today.

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:49.551
This is the

00:10:49.551 --> 00:10:53.101
spicy lobster-flavored chicken tenders.

00:10:53.101 --> 00:10:55.200
The Chinese says "yao yao,"

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:56.992
which means you have to shake it.

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:01.170
Oh, let's try these babies.

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:02.383
There was no need to shake it at all.

00:11:02.383 --> 00:11:04.160
There's no seasoning there at all.

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:07.443
It's just literally chicken tenders.

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:13.500
It's more of an aspiration
towards lobster, though.

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:15.900
And we've got crinkle-cut fries.

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:17.565
Oh, how I've missed you.

00:11:17.565 --> 00:11:20.160
Mm. Nothing beats a crinkle-cut fry.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:23.340
In China, we have a bunch
of different barrel options.

00:11:23.340 --> 00:11:27.660
For example, this one is
the Golden Arches bucket,

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:29.640
which actually didn't come in a bucket,

00:11:29.640 --> 00:11:31.740
they just put everything into a box.

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:34.620
The name actually is the
reason why we got this,

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:37.200
because McDonald's in China

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:40.277
has officially renamed to Jingongmen,

00:11:40.277 --> 00:11:42.300
which literally translates
as Golden Arches,

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:45.270
and when they did that
they caught a lot of flak.

00:11:45.270 --> 00:11:46.830
Everybody started laughing at them.

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:49.650
Nobody calls them the
Golden Arches in Chinese.

00:11:49.650 --> 00:11:51.180
It's just McDonald's.

00:11:51.180 --> 00:11:54.630
But legally they are now
known as the Golden Arches.

00:11:54.630 --> 00:11:58.170
Featuring sauces, you know
what that means, Yuelei.

00:11:58.170 --> 00:11:59.730
Sauce talk.

00:11:59.730 --> 00:12:02.490
Here are all of our exclusive sauces.

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:04.410
Garlic chili.

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:05.460
That's pretty much it.

00:12:05.460 --> 00:12:07.140
Oh, and no Sichuan sauce, either.

00:12:07.140 --> 00:12:08.310
That's an American invention,

00:12:08.310 --> 00:12:09.840
just like General Tso's chicken.

00:12:09.840 --> 00:12:12.810
But here in China, you
don't really get sauces

00:12:12.810 --> 00:12:15.660
unless you ask for them.
They come with the nuggets.

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:18.300
Chinese people expect food to be complete

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:19.590
when it arrives at your table.

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:22.200
You don't go and add more sauce to it.

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:25.059
Sauces. In the United
States, optimal for dipping.

00:12:25.059 --> 00:12:27.390
Tangy barbecue. Spicy Buffalo.

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:29.673
It's the USA, so you
know we got that ranch.

00:12:29.673 --> 00:12:30.698
Honey mustard.

00:12:30.698 --> 00:12:33.450
Honey, which is not here.
I don't know where it is.

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:35.970
Mayonnaise, which also
they did not include.

00:12:35.970 --> 00:12:38.190
Mexican-style salsa.

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:40.890
These are our exclusive desserts.

00:12:40.890 --> 00:12:43.050
I am going to try every
single one of them.

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:46.590
We can start with the taro pie.

00:12:46.590 --> 00:12:49.440
Taro is kind of like a cross

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:51.480
between sweet potato and potato.

00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:54.300
It's often used in desserts in Asia.

00:12:54.300 --> 00:12:58.173
You'll find them in everything
from pies to bubble tea.

00:12:59.430 --> 00:13:02.220
It's a bit like yam with a bit of jam,

00:13:02.220 --> 00:13:03.660
but it's subtly sweet.

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:06.210
For Chinese people, if you say
a dessert is not very sweet,

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:07.380
that's actually a compliment.

00:13:07.380 --> 00:13:10.713
Pineapple pie, also one of my favorites.

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:15.528
Mm. That is heavenly.

00:13:15.528 --> 00:13:16.768
I think I'm going to finish this.

00:13:16.768 --> 00:13:19.110
Now I need to chew for a very long time.

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:22.650
So, here we've got the strawberry sundae,

00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:24.120
which is kind of melted already,

00:13:24.120 --> 00:13:26.940
but I'm sure it would've been
amazing when it first arrived.

00:13:26.940 --> 00:13:30.270
An affogato and a
matcha-flavored affogato,

00:13:30.270 --> 00:13:33.360
and then here we've got the McFlurrys.

00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:36.727
This is the strawberry McFlurry

00:13:36.727 --> 00:13:39.076
with Oreo cookies.

00:13:39.076 --> 00:13:43.650
Oh, my gosh, that is perhaps
the most sinful thing

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:44.880
that you could have.

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:47.310
Oh, but it's so good.

00:13:47.310 --> 00:13:49.530
This is just the regular McFlurry,

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:52.050
and here is my all-time favorite,

00:13:52.050 --> 00:13:55.950
mango-pomelo-sago-flavored McFlurry.

00:13:55.950 --> 00:13:58.530
Hm. It's very different
with the ice cream.

00:13:58.530 --> 00:14:00.985
You still got the mango in there,

00:14:00.985 --> 00:14:04.320
and the pomelo, it's
very juicy, it's tender,

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:06.120
like little tiny pips in there

00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:07.800
that kind of pop when you eat them.

00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:09.063
Oh! Just perfect.

00:14:10.259 --> 00:14:12.720
Mm. Brain freeze. Oh!

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:13.980
In the US, you can get yourself

00:14:13.980 --> 00:14:16.710
a McFlurry with mini M&amp;M's.

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:21.360
For some reason, mini M&amp;M's
taste better than regular M&amp;M's.

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:24.240
I love mini M&amp;M's. Mm.

00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:25.852
Hot caramel sundae.

00:14:25.852 --> 00:14:28.080
It's classic. They don't
have this in China?

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:31.710
God, I mean, what's more
American than an apple pie?

00:14:31.710 --> 00:14:33.900
Look at this thing. Let's
crack that bad boy open.

00:14:33.900 --> 00:14:35.682
We got chocolate chip cookies.

00:14:35.682 --> 00:14:37.650
Shakes. You can get three
different types of shakes

00:14:37.650 --> 00:14:39.783
here at a US McDonald's. Chocolate.

00:14:41.070 --> 00:14:42.028
Classic chocolate.

00:14:42.028 --> 00:14:43.586
Strawberry, personal favorite.

00:14:44.460 --> 00:14:45.630
That's so good.

00:14:45.630 --> 00:14:47.580
Vanilla, the classic.

00:14:47.580 --> 00:14:51.750
Our exclusive drinks
include the Fuze iced tea.

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:55.260
We've got the Minute Maid orange McFloat,

00:14:55.260 --> 00:14:57.626
bubble tea, soy milk,

00:14:57.626 --> 00:15:00.151
pure milk, Ceylon black tea,

00:15:00.151 --> 00:15:02.580
which in China we would call red tea,

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:05.010
which just confuses you for fun.

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:07.290
I'm going to go back to here

00:15:07.290 --> 00:15:09.327
because this is the
only thing I want to try

00:15:09.327 --> 00:15:10.310
out of all of them.

00:15:12.240 --> 00:15:13.620
That tastes like orange juice.

00:15:13.620 --> 00:15:15.442
It's just plain old orange juice.

00:15:15.442 --> 00:15:17.430
In the US, you can get
yourself a Dr Pepper,

00:15:17.430 --> 00:15:21.147
a Fanta orange and an
Orange Lavaburst, lemonade.

00:15:21.147 --> 00:15:23.400
You can also get frozen drinks.

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:26.610
You can get a frozen Fanta
blue raspberry or frozen Coke.

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:28.290
McDonald's also has smoothies.

00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:32.340
A mango pineapple smoothie
and a strawberry smoothie.

00:15:32.340 --> 00:15:34.230
Yeah, they make a decent
smoothie at McDonald's.

00:15:34.230 --> 00:15:35.063
As you can see,

00:15:35.063 --> 00:15:38.250
we have an absolute ton of
breakfast options here in China.

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:41.130
I think McDonald's has done
fantastic in this regard

00:15:41.130 --> 00:15:45.270
because the Chinese treat
breakfast as a very special meal.

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:46.720
We have a very similar saying to,

00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:48.670
"Eat breakfast like a king,

00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:51.180
lunch like a prince,
dinner like a pauper."

00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:55.290
So, starting with the
sausage McMuffin with egg.

00:15:55.290 --> 00:15:56.520
Always a good way to start the day.

00:15:56.520 --> 00:15:59.910
You can get this as a double as well.

00:15:59.910 --> 00:16:02.100
Next we have the ham muffin.

00:16:02.100 --> 00:16:04.800
It's just literally a piece of ham,

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:06.570
some lettuce, and two muffins,

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:09.510
so I guess this would
actually be a hamburger.

00:16:09.510 --> 00:16:11.250
You can get this as a double as well.

00:16:11.250 --> 00:16:14.133
Next we have the grilled chicken muffin.

00:16:17.340 --> 00:16:19.620
This chicken's been
sitting around for a while.

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:23.970
Next we've got the
crispy chicken McMuffin.

00:16:23.970 --> 00:16:28.965
So this is the breakfast version of the

00:16:28.965 --> 00:16:31.020
"such a big chicken chop."

00:16:31.020 --> 00:16:35.040
Breakfast in the US. We have
so many breakfast options,

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:37.050
starting down here, the sandwiches.

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:39.270
Egg McMuffin. Maybe the first

00:16:39.270 --> 00:16:41.400
fast breakfast sandwich
to ever hit the market.

00:16:41.400 --> 00:16:43.410
Sausage McMuffin. Sausage and cheese.

00:16:43.410 --> 00:16:44.370
If you hadn't noticed,

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:46.920
this is all on what we
call an English muffin,

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:48.330
'cause they're from England.

00:16:48.330 --> 00:16:50.550
There's also a bacon,
egg, and cheese McMuffin.

00:16:50.550 --> 00:16:53.220
But the option that we have most for

00:16:53.220 --> 00:16:55.770
are the scrambled-egg burgers.

00:16:55.770 --> 00:16:57.690
Scrambled-egg grilled chicken burger.

00:16:57.690 --> 00:17:02.430
The scrambled egg is
very luminously yellow.

00:17:02.430 --> 00:17:03.643
Wow, look at that.

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:06.660
Very peppery.

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:08.340
They love their pepper here, don't they?

00:17:08.340 --> 00:17:10.620
So, the scrambled-egg sausage burger.

00:17:10.620 --> 00:17:12.150
You'll notice the buns are different now.

00:17:12.150 --> 00:17:14.430
We're no longer on the muffins.
We're back to regular buns.

00:17:14.430 --> 00:17:16.530
Oh, it's squeezing out, isn't it?

00:17:16.530 --> 00:17:19.050
Scrambled-egg cheeseburger.

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:22.410
This is the brightest burger
I've ever seen in my life.

00:17:22.410 --> 00:17:24.030
It's definitely very portable.

00:17:24.030 --> 00:17:26.130
I think that's one thing that
McDonald's has done very well,

00:17:26.130 --> 00:17:29.760
because Chinese breakfast
traditionally is not too portable

00:17:29.760 --> 00:17:32.220
in the sense that you need to
sit down to a lot of meals,

00:17:32.220 --> 00:17:35.100
like if you want to eat
wonton in the morning

00:17:35.100 --> 00:17:36.930
or if you want to eat
some soups in the morning.

00:17:36.930 --> 00:17:38.430
This you can just take and go.

00:17:38.430 --> 00:17:41.550
And, of course, you can
get the scrambled-egg

00:17:41.550 --> 00:17:44.580
German-flavor-sausage burger.

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:45.660
Oh, at least they give you two,

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:48.540
as opposed to just one tiny sausage.

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:50.790
Biscuits, biscuits, biscuits.

00:17:50.790 --> 00:17:52.080
Sausage and egg biscuit.

00:17:52.080 --> 00:17:54.450
So, the biscuits are the
same breakfast sandwiches

00:17:54.450 --> 00:17:56.340
you get in English-muffin form,

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:59.010
but in this biscuit form,
the American biscuit,

00:17:59.010 --> 00:18:02.040
this dry, crumbly, buttery biscuit,

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:04.530
there is a bacon, egg, and cheese one.

00:18:04.530 --> 00:18:06.840
For some reason people in this country

00:18:06.840 --> 00:18:11.280
seem to want just a biscuit and sausage

00:18:11.280 --> 00:18:12.990
with no sauce, no nothing.

00:18:12.990 --> 00:18:16.410
This is as dry as if
you'd go into a barbershop

00:18:16.410 --> 00:18:18.450
and take a handful of hair clippings

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:21.690
and just shove them in your
mouth. This is that dry.

00:18:21.690 --> 00:18:24.477
In the US we have something
called McGriddles,

00:18:24.477 --> 00:18:26.370
and McGriddles are breakfast sandwiches

00:18:26.370 --> 00:18:29.760
where they replace the
English muffin and/or biscuit

00:18:29.760 --> 00:18:31.290
with pancakes.

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:33.270
So, first of all, they got the
McDonald's logo right there.

00:18:33.270 --> 00:18:34.470
Too hilarious.

00:18:34.470 --> 00:18:36.765
Somehow, through the miracle of science,

00:18:36.765 --> 00:18:40.330
was able to inject syrup
into these pancakes.

00:18:41.962 --> 00:18:42.953
Sensational.

00:18:42.953 --> 00:18:46.350
You can get your McGriddles
in sausage, egg, and cheese

00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:47.533
and then just sausage.

00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:52.440
On to what I was going to
talk about, the congee.

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:55.260
Congee is a very traditional
breakfast item here in China.

00:18:55.260 --> 00:18:57.390
It's basically just rice porridge,

00:18:57.390 --> 00:18:59.760
and it's something that is

00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:02.850
kind of like chicken
soup for Chinese people,

00:19:02.850 --> 00:19:04.980
in the sense that if you fall ill,

00:19:04.980 --> 00:19:07.980
you're going to be given one
of these, plain, with nothing.

00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:11.070
This I think is with century egg,

00:19:11.070 --> 00:19:14.430
but the century egg,
it tastes a little bit

00:19:14.430 --> 00:19:16.440
like a blue-cheese version of egg,

00:19:16.440 --> 00:19:19.380
in that it's kind of
like egg that's gone off,

00:19:19.380 --> 00:19:20.850
but in a very nice way.

00:19:20.850 --> 00:19:24.180
And this adds a nice
savoriness to the congee.

00:19:24.180 --> 00:19:26.880
You can also get it with

00:19:26.880 --> 00:19:29.546
pickles and bamboo shoots.

00:19:29.546 --> 00:19:31.320
And if you're going to get congee,

00:19:31.320 --> 00:19:32.760
then usually you need to pair it

00:19:32.760 --> 00:19:36.060
with what they've called
an "Asian dough stick."

00:19:36.060 --> 00:19:38.100
This is what we call a youtiao,

00:19:38.100 --> 00:19:41.100
which is literally a stick of fried dough.

00:19:41.100 --> 00:19:43.230
These are absolutely amazing

00:19:43.230 --> 00:19:45.690
when paired with stuff like soy milk

00:19:45.690 --> 00:19:47.553
and, of course, with congee.

00:19:48.570 --> 00:19:50.370
You know, you need to eat these fresh.

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:53.267
Deep-fried, they are so incredibly crispy.

00:19:53.267 --> 00:19:55.500
Oh, wow, well done, McDonald's.

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:57.870
Like, 10 hours later,
these are still crispy.

00:19:57.870 --> 00:20:00.510
I'm very impressed but
also a little bit worried

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:03.360
because they should never be
this crispy after that long.

00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:05.280
I wonder what they've put in here.

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:07.860
Last but not least, our
German sausages again.

00:20:07.860 --> 00:20:09.270
It's not just sandwiches, you guys.

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:12.793
We also have something in the US,

00:20:12.793 --> 00:20:15.657
the Big Breakfast, which
is totally in disarray.

00:20:15.657 --> 00:20:18.006
This is like the advertising
for this breakfast.

00:20:18.006 --> 00:20:19.639
I'm sorry?

00:20:19.639 --> 00:20:22.658
The Big Breakfast with pancakes.

00:20:22.658 --> 00:20:24.960
You can also get hotcakes, aka pancakes.

00:20:24.960 --> 00:20:27.900
There's no way they're back
there, like, ladling the ...

00:20:27.900 --> 00:20:29.910
right? There's no way they're doing that.

00:20:29.910 --> 00:20:31.950
These have to be premade and
they just heat them up, right?

00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:33.300
So, hotcakes and sausage.

00:20:33.300 --> 00:20:34.890
Oh, and they both come with syrup,

00:20:34.890 --> 00:20:36.246
so you know what we gotta do.

00:20:36.246 --> 00:20:39.840
Oh-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho, yeah!

00:20:39.840 --> 00:20:42.081
We also have a

00:20:42.081 --> 00:20:45.997
morning wrap with ham.

00:20:45.997 --> 00:20:49.290
The wrap itself is basically frozen solid.

00:20:49.290 --> 00:20:53.748
We can exchange that with sausage,

00:20:53.748 --> 00:20:55.148
which is also frozen.

00:20:55.148 --> 00:20:57.090
It's almost like a piece of art now,

00:20:57.090 --> 00:20:59.700
like you're supposed to look
at it instead of eating it.

00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:01.500
Wow, frozen in time.

00:21:01.500 --> 00:21:04.091
US McDonald's have

00:21:04.091 --> 00:21:06.900
sausage breakfast burritos.

00:21:06.900 --> 00:21:07.941
I mean, I can't even unfold,

00:21:07.941 --> 00:21:09.282
I'm just, like, ripping it apart.

00:21:09.282 --> 00:21:11.610
You got scrambled eggs, the sausage,

00:21:11.610 --> 00:21:13.830
it comes with Mexican-style salsa.

00:21:13.830 --> 00:21:15.120
Hey, McDonald's, it's actually pretty good

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:16.530
considering that this is, like,

00:21:16.530 --> 00:21:19.650
probably the furthest
you can get from salsa

00:21:19.650 --> 00:21:21.390
and still legally be
able to call it salsa.

00:21:21.390 --> 00:21:23.580
If you're not trying to
completely destroy your insides

00:21:23.580 --> 00:21:24.450
first thing in the morning,

00:21:24.450 --> 00:21:27.180
you can get yourself
fruit and maple oatmeal.

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:28.170
Seems like your breakfast

00:21:28.170 --> 00:21:30.600
is trying to escape
your body an hour later,

00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:32.190
might actually be able to hold this down.

00:21:32.190 --> 00:21:36.000
Et voilà, ze options from le bakery.

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:37.440
So, we have macarons.

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:39.300
Right now we have two different flavors,

00:21:39.300 --> 00:21:42.660
chocolate and berries.

00:21:42.660 --> 00:21:44.660
These actually look really legit.

00:21:46.410 --> 00:21:49.260
Pat yourself on the back.
This is really good.

00:21:49.260 --> 00:21:51.720
And these things are lamingtons.

00:21:51.720 --> 00:21:53.640
I've never actually had lamingtons.

00:21:53.640 --> 00:21:57.120
Apparently, they're basically
Australian sponge cakes

00:21:57.120 --> 00:21:59.280
which are covered in coconut flakes,

00:21:59.280 --> 00:22:01.443
and this is a lemon-flavored one.

00:22:02.400 --> 00:22:04.232
Surprisingly addictive.

00:22:04.232 --> 00:22:06.600
We have the McCafé bakery.

00:22:06.600 --> 00:22:10.500
At the McCafé bakery, you
get, you know, sweet treats,

00:22:10.500 --> 00:22:11.790
not necessarily for breakfast

00:22:11.790 --> 00:22:13.650
but probably leaning more
towards breakfast time.

00:22:13.650 --> 00:22:15.990
Ba-bam, blueberry muffin.

00:22:15.990 --> 00:22:19.170
A cinnamon roll with
cream cheese frosting.

00:22:19.170 --> 00:22:22.590
It looks like it's squishy.
It most certainly is not.

00:22:22.590 --> 00:22:25.110
I mean, come on, who doesn't
love an apple fritter?

00:22:25.110 --> 00:22:27.630
An apple fritter is a doughnut
that tastes like apple

00:22:27.630 --> 00:22:31.200
and is shaped like it was
just squoze in someone's hand

00:22:31.200 --> 00:22:32.430
for some strange reason.

00:22:32.430 --> 00:22:36.810
These are our McCafé drink options,

00:22:36.810 --> 00:22:41.430
starting with the extra-milky
latte with oat milk.

00:22:41.430 --> 00:22:43.170
A latte is two-thirds milk,

00:22:43.170 --> 00:22:44.370
and then you add oat milk in there,

00:22:44.370 --> 00:22:47.250
I don't think we're going
to have much coffee.

00:22:47.250 --> 00:22:50.130
Oh. Oh, wow, that is surprisingly good.

00:22:50.130 --> 00:22:52.470
In China, oat milk has
really, really taken off

00:22:52.470 --> 00:22:55.350
because a lot of people did
not grow up drinking milk.

00:22:55.350 --> 00:22:57.840
A lot of Chinese people
are lactose intolerant.

00:22:57.840 --> 00:23:01.830
And so oat milk is definitely
a very healthy alternative,

00:23:01.830 --> 00:23:03.390
and that's why we have the

00:23:03.390 --> 00:23:06.090
extra-strong chocolate with oat milk.

00:23:06.090 --> 00:23:08.160
You can also get this without oat milk.

00:23:08.160 --> 00:23:10.144
Extra-strong matcha milk.

00:23:10.144 --> 00:23:11.301
Extra-strong matcha --

00:23:11.301 --> 00:23:13.830
oh, we have so much matcha.

00:23:13.830 --> 00:23:16.680
Extra-strong chocolate smoothie,

00:23:16.680 --> 00:23:20.490
extra-strong milk and vanilla smoothie,

00:23:20.490 --> 00:23:25.229
and the matcha milk with matcha jelly.

00:23:25.229 --> 00:23:27.510
Matcha, matcha, oh, I'm going to --

00:23:27.510 --> 00:23:31.413
We absolutely love matcha here
in China. I don't know why.

00:23:32.700 --> 00:23:36.120
It tastes like grass and frozen grass.

00:23:36.120 --> 00:23:39.210
Coffees and coffees and
coffees and coffees.

00:23:39.210 --> 00:23:43.560
McDonald's has a assortment
of featured drinks,

00:23:43.560 --> 00:23:46.770
espresso drinks, mochas, iced lattes.

00:23:46.770 --> 00:23:47.940
Let's get all that on the screen.

00:23:47.940 --> 00:23:49.620
See? All these things.

00:23:49.620 --> 00:23:51.995
This is the cold brew. This is so strong.

00:23:53.340 --> 00:23:54.960
I think each of you should
eventually take a sip.

00:23:54.960 --> 00:23:57.095
You will not believe how
strong the cold brew is.

00:23:57.095 --> 00:23:59.040
Oh, my God.

00:23:59.040 --> 00:24:00.090
French vanilla latte.

00:24:00.990 --> 00:24:03.420
This is the exact
opposite. This is so sweet.

00:24:03.420 --> 00:24:05.520
Mocha. Who doesn't want hot chocolate

00:24:05.520 --> 00:24:06.930
first thing in the morning?

00:24:06.930 --> 00:24:08.430
Hilarious, people are buying that.

00:24:08.430 --> 00:24:10.770
Ooh, this is the premium roast coffee.

00:24:10.770 --> 00:24:11.880
I know I've been kind of dissing on it,

00:24:11.880 --> 00:24:14.250
but their actual coffee, the
actual McDonald's coffee,

00:24:14.250 --> 00:24:15.390
I think is very good.

00:24:15.390 --> 00:24:17.533
They're a good contender in
the coffee game, I think,

00:24:17.533 --> 00:24:18.630
in the fast-food coffee game.

00:24:18.630 --> 00:24:20.370
Especially the horrible
PR nightmare they had

00:24:20.370 --> 00:24:22.380
when they, like, destroyed
that lady's crotch

00:24:22.380 --> 00:24:23.670
with their superhot coffee.

00:24:23.670 --> 00:24:25.650
It is a comeback story, McDonald's.

00:24:25.650 --> 00:24:28.110
Almost killing a woman
with second-degree burns

00:24:28.110 --> 00:24:29.490
from boiling-hot coffee

00:24:29.490 --> 00:24:32.400
to these nice little fun café drinks.

00:24:32.400 --> 00:24:35.280
I would happily pour
this all over my crotch.

00:24:35.280 --> 00:24:37.260
You can get the iced-coffee drinks.

00:24:37.260 --> 00:24:38.940
Don't like this. This is the mocha.

00:24:38.940 --> 00:24:43.860
McDonald's in China also
has a late-night menu.

00:24:43.860 --> 00:24:46.322
They only have one item,
but this is worth it.

00:24:46.322 --> 00:24:50.560
I got it last night. These
are marinated chicken bones.

00:24:50.560 --> 00:24:51.660
They don't sound very appealing,

00:24:51.660 --> 00:24:54.990
but the Chinese name
is wordplay on an idiom

00:24:54.990 --> 00:24:59.190
which kind of means "the
highest level of artistry."

00:24:59.190 --> 00:25:01.945
And when I opened up this box,

00:25:01.945 --> 00:25:03.630
[gasps]

00:25:03.630 --> 00:25:06.510
I literally heard angels going, "Aah!"

00:25:06.510 --> 00:25:10.140
This is actually a street food

00:25:10.140 --> 00:25:14.220
from someplace up in Northeast
China called Shenyang.

00:25:14.220 --> 00:25:16.020
Chinese people love fiddly stuff,

00:25:16.020 --> 00:25:19.173
and meat on the bone is
just that much more tasty.

00:25:21.030 --> 00:25:23.700
Ah, still incredible, even cold.

00:25:23.700 --> 00:25:27.120
You know, the box actually
says "marinated chicken bones."

00:25:27.120 --> 00:25:29.660
"Be careful, it may contain bones."

00:25:29.660 --> 00:25:32.310
And you're actually supposed
to spit the bones out,

00:25:32.310 --> 00:25:35.700
but I'm having so much
fun eating this thing,

00:25:35.700 --> 00:25:37.680
I actually eat the bones too.

00:25:37.680 --> 00:25:41.280
It's spicy, it's sour, it's sweet.

00:25:41.280 --> 00:25:43.770
Ah, and just absolutely divine.

00:25:43.770 --> 00:25:46.258
I can see how people would be
inspired after eating this.

00:25:48.300 --> 00:25:51.300
So, McDonald's came to China in 1990,

00:25:51.300 --> 00:25:54.120
and then it opened in Beijing in '92.

00:25:54.120 --> 00:25:56.760
Back then, that was the largest
McDonald's in the world.

00:25:56.760 --> 00:25:58.470
They had 700 seats.

00:25:58.470 --> 00:26:02.520
On opening day, they served 40,000 people.

00:26:02.520 --> 00:26:03.960
And people didn't go there for the food.

00:26:03.960 --> 00:26:05.760
It was a place to be seen.

00:26:05.760 --> 00:26:08.490
Like, McDonald's was a window to the West.

00:26:08.490 --> 00:26:10.650
It was a cosmopolitan place

00:26:10.650 --> 00:26:14.910
to experience capitalism, in a way.

00:26:14.910 --> 00:26:18.270
But over time it became
a trendy hangout spot

00:26:18.270 --> 00:26:19.770
for city kids after school.

00:26:19.770 --> 00:26:21.360
They'd go there to do their homework.

00:26:21.360 --> 00:26:24.540
It still very much is middle class.

00:26:24.540 --> 00:26:28.380
I remember actually when I came
to visit China 20 years ago,

00:26:28.380 --> 00:26:32.550
my aunts greeted me at the
airport with bags of McDonald's,

00:26:32.550 --> 00:26:35.160
and I was actually kind of offended

00:26:35.160 --> 00:26:38.190
that they would bring junk food to meet me

00:26:38.190 --> 00:26:39.540
as opposed to real Chinese food,

00:26:39.540 --> 00:26:42.720
but for them McDonald's
was the best of the best.

00:26:42.720 --> 00:26:45.150
It was all the prestige.

00:26:45.150 --> 00:26:47.520
Hey, to me, McDonald's,
when it comes to fast food,

00:26:47.520 --> 00:26:50.940
is No. 1 in the US, dare I say the world.

00:26:50.940 --> 00:26:52.680
If you just want a good hot meal

00:26:52.680 --> 00:26:54.240
where you know exactly what
it's going to taste like

00:26:54.240 --> 00:26:57.030
and get it and go, McDonald's never fails.

00:26:57.030 --> 00:26:58.950
Waiting in line, getting
it at the drive-through,

00:26:58.950 --> 00:27:00.270
you get it lickety-split.

00:27:00.270 --> 00:27:03.258
Now they leaned really big
into delivery since COVID,

00:27:03.258 --> 00:27:06.090
and, man, McDonald's is
showing up right away,

00:27:06.090 --> 00:27:08.280
and I love it. It's dangerous.

00:27:08.280 --> 00:27:09.113
I can't remember the last time

00:27:09.113 --> 00:27:11.070
I've eaten inside at a McDonald's.

00:27:11.070 --> 00:27:13.200
So, I usually dine in at McDonald's,

00:27:13.200 --> 00:27:16.350
but I find that in China
they focus more on delivery,

00:27:16.350 --> 00:27:18.120
and they promise to get
everything delivered

00:27:18.120 --> 00:27:21.030
within 30 minutes, which
they actually keep to,

00:27:21.030 --> 00:27:22.680
and that's incredibly impressive.

00:27:22.680 --> 00:27:24.870
Last night I ordered the chicken carcass.

00:27:24.870 --> 00:27:26.820
It took 28 minutes.

00:27:26.820 --> 00:27:29.040
Got a Big Mac earlier.
That was 10 minutes.

00:27:29.040 --> 00:27:31.260
So they're very, very punctual.

00:27:31.260 --> 00:27:33.210
They're also open for very long,

00:27:33.210 --> 00:27:34.950
from 7 till 10 p.m.,

00:27:34.950 --> 00:27:36.630
and there are many 24-hour branches,

00:27:36.630 --> 00:27:38.640
so extremely convenient.

00:27:38.640 --> 00:27:40.620
Now, McDonald's is an American brand,

00:27:40.620 --> 00:27:43.230
so they have American
classics on the menu,

00:27:43.230 --> 00:27:45.510
hamburgers, chicken sandwiches,

00:27:45.510 --> 00:27:48.420
but they kind of
assimilated and made popular

00:27:48.420 --> 00:27:50.100
the burger culture in this country.

00:27:50.100 --> 00:27:51.360
It's hard to say, because I feel like

00:27:51.360 --> 00:27:53.130
the American taste is McDonald's.

00:27:53.130 --> 00:27:54.810
I think McDonald's has actually adapted

00:27:54.810 --> 00:27:56.730
pretty well to Chinese tastes.

00:27:56.730 --> 00:27:59.310
Besides the McSpicy burger and wings

00:27:59.310 --> 00:28:01.020
and the grilled chicken sandwich,

00:28:01.020 --> 00:28:03.060
which have all become bestsellers,

00:28:03.060 --> 00:28:05.880
McDonald's actually
uses chicken thigh meat

00:28:05.880 --> 00:28:08.700
instead of breast meat in
all of its chicken burgers,

00:28:08.700 --> 00:28:10.251
except for the McChicken.

00:28:10.251 --> 00:28:11.863
And I think that's because Chinese people

00:28:11.863 --> 00:28:14.220
think chicken breast is dry,

00:28:14.220 --> 00:28:17.160
and they've also got lots
of time-limited specials

00:28:17.160 --> 00:28:21.060
when it comes to the desserts,
like the mantou burger,

00:28:21.060 --> 00:28:23.010
which is kind of like a Chinese bun,

00:28:23.010 --> 00:28:25.170
and even cilantro sundae.

00:28:25.170 --> 00:28:27.150
McDonald's, everyone's
going after McDonald's.

00:28:27.150 --> 00:28:28.710
Burger King's been going after McDonald's

00:28:28.710 --> 00:28:30.300
since, what, the '60s?

00:28:30.300 --> 00:28:31.590
Every burger chain

00:28:31.590 --> 00:28:34.710
try to get some sort
of edge on McDonald's.

00:28:34.710 --> 00:28:38.520
We're fancier, we got
different varieties of stuff.

00:28:38.520 --> 00:28:41.850
McDonald's is No. 1,
here, now, and forever.

00:28:41.850 --> 00:28:44.910
The McDonald's logo should be
on the American flag, dammit!

00:28:44.910 --> 00:28:48.240
So, China is McDonald's
second-largest market

00:28:48.240 --> 00:28:50.220
by store count, after the US.

00:28:50.220 --> 00:28:54.840
In China, there are over
5,000 McDonald's locations,

00:28:54.840 --> 00:28:58.110
but KFC has over 9,000.

00:28:58.110 --> 00:28:59.220
They actually came here first,

00:28:59.220 --> 00:29:02.250
so it's KFC, then McDonald's,

00:29:02.250 --> 00:29:04.590
then a local brand called Dicos,

00:29:04.590 --> 00:29:07.710
which does both fried chicken and burgers,

00:29:07.710 --> 00:29:10.510
so they're really just
fighting an uphill battle.

00:29:12.780 --> 00:29:15.703
In China, a Big Mac costs 25 yuan.

00:29:15.703 --> 00:29:18.450
A Big Mac in the US costs $5.29.

00:29:18.450 --> 00:29:19.470
Make it a Big Mac meal

00:29:19.470 --> 00:29:24.360
with a medium fries and
medium Coke, and it's 36 yuan.

00:29:24.360 --> 00:29:27.030
If you want to go large,
that's 4 yuan extra

00:29:27.030 --> 00:29:29.670
for a grand total of 40 yuan.

00:29:29.670 --> 00:29:30.503
If you make it a meal

00:29:30.503 --> 00:29:32.070
with a medium fries and medium drink,

00:29:32.070 --> 00:29:34.920
price goes up to $9.29.

00:29:34.920 --> 00:29:38.850
Upgrade that to a large, and it's $10.79.

00:29:38.850 --> 00:29:42.810
Our Big Mac large meal costs 86% more.

00:29:42.810 --> 00:29:44.940
So our Big Mac meal is cheaper,

00:29:44.940 --> 00:29:48.180
but at the same time
the average daily wage

00:29:48.180 --> 00:29:52.230
of a cabby in Beijing is
about 200 yuan, give or take,

00:29:52.230 --> 00:29:55.680
and so this would be 20% of their salary.

00:29:55.680 --> 00:29:57.150
So it's still not really something

00:29:57.150 --> 00:30:00.233
that you would eat on a regular
basis, but maybe splurge on.

00:30:02.550 --> 00:30:03.630
Let's talk nutrition.

00:30:03.630 --> 00:30:05.618
This is that very Big Mac, again.

00:30:05.618 --> 00:30:08.201
In the US, it's 590 calories

00:30:08.201 --> 00:30:09.626
and all this stuff.

00:30:09.626 --> 00:30:14.040
In China, our Big Mac has 524 calories,

00:30:14.040 --> 00:30:17.640
26 grams of fat, 45 grams of carbs,

00:30:17.640 --> 00:30:19.840
27 grams of protein,

00:30:19.840 --> 00:30:23.131
and 877 milligrams of sodium.

00:30:23.131 --> 00:30:24.480
What if we did a combo?

00:30:24.480 --> 00:30:27.120
Starting with the medium fries,

00:30:27.120 --> 00:30:29.495
this adds 320 calories to the meal,

00:30:29.495 --> 00:30:30.728
and all this stuff.

00:30:30.728 --> 00:30:34.740
While a medium fries in
China contains 290 calories,

00:30:34.740 --> 00:30:37.156
13 grams of total fat,

00:30:37.156 --> 00:30:40.147
35.9 grams of carbs,

00:30:40.147 --> 00:30:42.480
we're not sure if it contains any sugars,

00:30:42.480 --> 00:30:43.788
4 grams of protein,

00:30:43.788 --> 00:30:47.829
and 252 milligrams of sodium.

00:30:47.829 --> 00:30:49.470
But you need something to drink.

00:30:49.470 --> 00:30:50.880
Add in a medium Coke to that,

00:30:50.880 --> 00:30:54.600
and this kicks your meal
up another 210 calories.

00:30:54.600 --> 00:30:55.590
We'll do the same.

00:30:55.590 --> 00:30:58.410
Here's everything in a
medium Coke in China.

00:30:58.410 --> 00:31:01.680
148 calories. That leaves the grand total

00:31:01.680 --> 00:31:06.210
for the China meal at 962 calories.

00:31:06.210 --> 00:31:08.370
While in the US, the total
ends up looking like this.

00:31:08.370 --> 00:31:12.390
1,120 calories and all this other stuff.

00:31:12.390 --> 00:31:14.298
Get a load of that sodium, though.

00:31:14.298 --> 00:31:15.281
Guh!

00:31:15.281 --> 00:31:17.550
Take the box out. You
can't throw away the box.

00:31:17.550 --> 00:31:18.630
Some kind of hoop.

00:31:18.630 --> 00:31:21.060
Just trying to build
some more Yao Mings here.

00:31:21.060 --> 00:31:22.950
Give me a couple decades.

00:31:22.950 --> 00:31:25.560
Now, usually when a foreign
brand comes to China,

00:31:25.560 --> 00:31:27.510
they get a Chinese name too,

00:31:27.510 --> 00:31:29.430
and sometimes it's a transliteration,

00:31:29.430 --> 00:31:32.160
and sometimes they get
really nice meanings as well.

00:31:32.160 --> 00:31:35.430
For McDonald's, the
Chinese name is Maidanglao,

00:31:35.430 --> 00:31:37.020
which is a transliteration,

00:31:37.020 --> 00:31:39.822
but you could also kind
of take it to mean that

00:31:39.822 --> 00:31:43.357
wheat is obligated to work for you.

